intonation: no special exclamation phrase (drop IBM's)

exclam_phrase still matches a sentence ending in `!' and succeeds, but
no longer copies IBM's exclamation values over the phrase-final fields
(2048 to 2040, 2116 to 2386). The generic sentence-final path then
processes the utterance the way it processes any other terminator,
the way period_phrase already matches-and-succeeds with no assignment
of its own. The mark itself is untouched: a mark-less utterance still
wedges the engine, so `!' stays in the text.

diff --git a/lang/enus/rules/ut_inton.dr b/lang/enus/rules/ut_inton.dr
--- a/lang/enus/rules/ut_inton.dr
+++ b/lang/enus/rules/ut_inton.dr
@@ -4387,9 +4387,5 @@
   call precedes_end_quote arity 2 depth 3
   popn 3
   cmp testl reg r0 reg r0
   branch jne to L7
-  load movw ind reg r6 2048 into r0w
-  store movw reg r0w ind reg r6 2040
-  load movw ind reg r6 2116 into r0w
-  store movw reg r0w ind reg r6 2386
 label L7 was at_0x11a
   push reg r6
   call succeed arity 1 depth 1
